{
  "rule_id": "ya_idafa_fath",
  "version": "1",
  "name_ar": "فتح ياء الإضافة قبل الهمزة",
  "definition": "Qaloun opens (fatha) the first-person ya before every hamza qat' and before hamzat al-wasl, with the exceptions in the next record.",
  "riwaya": "qaloun",
  "tariq": "unspecified",
  "family": "ya_idafa",
  "detectability": "B",
  "limitations": [
    "Paraphrase of the cited pages by an automated drafter; not scholarly reviewed.",
    "Only Book A is cited; the printed page is where the section begins and needs proofreading.",
    "Recognised from the open ya the corpus spells with a fatha; the third-person pronoun هي is skipped.",
    "Book A p.47 item 1 gives « عهدي الظالمين » at al-Baqara 144; the word is in the Kufian ayah 2:124 in the corpus and not in 2:144. The number is the book's error and has no effect here, since this rule is read from the spelling and not from a place.",
    "Second citation: the longer book Nabhan, which Book A digests. It agrees with the paraphrase, so it shows where the text is found, not an independent confirmation."
  ],
